    "result_text": "All 54 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did to replace the level rules with the points system:\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 replaced the old direct-level computation with:\n- A new `membershipPoints(owner)` method: starts at `0`, `+2` for a present email, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, and `+3` when tenure exceeds 365 days.\n- A rewritten `membershipLevel(owner)` that maps points \u2192 level: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n- Added the `@Mapping(target = \"membershipPoints\", ...)` so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field to the Owner schema and updated the `membershipLevel` description/bounds (max is now `4`); the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time.\n\nThe existing `householdMemberCount` (already populated at creation as household members + 1) drives the household-of-3 rule, so the third household member with an email scores 5 points \u2192 level 3 (Cp23/Cp39), and a fresh unique owner with an email scores 3 \u2192 level 2 (Cp15/Cp24/Cp40). A new owner's zero tenure keeps them capped below level 4 as required.",
