    "probe_text": "Here is the exact ordered sequence for `addOwner` (POST `/api/owners`), reading top-to-bottom through `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (lines 529\u2013565).\n\n## Gate (before the method body)\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected before anything else runs.\n\n## In-order steps inside the method\n\n1. **Normalize address (side-effect on the DTO)** \u2014 `setAddress(normalizeAddress(...))`. Trims, collapses internal whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands street-type abbreviations word-by-word (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A `null`/blank address becomes `\"\"`. This *mutates the incoming DTO before validation*, so a blank address becomes `\"\"` \u2014 which then fails the required-field check below.\n\n2. **Required-fields validation** \u2014 `validateRequiredFields`. Rejects (`RequiredFieldsMissingException`, listing offending fields) if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is missing/blank. (Runs *after* step 1, so address is checked in its normalized form.)\n\n3. **Postcode validation** \u2014 `validatePostcode(postcode, city)`. Postcode is optional; `null` is accepted. If present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown city \u2192 any 4-digit value accepted. Violations throw `InvalidFieldsException([\"postcode\"])`.\n\n4. **Telephone normalization + validation** \u2014 `normalizeTelephone(...)` (result held in a local, not yet applied). Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`/country code, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; result must be `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, and must satisfy the country-specific national length (AU `61`\u21929 national digits, NANP `1`\u219210). Failures throw `InvalidFieldsException([\"telephone\"])`.\n\n5. **City capacity check** \u2014 `requireCityHasCapacity(city)`. Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 50 throws `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n6. **Email normalization + validation** \u2014 `normalizeEmail(...)`. Email is optional; `null`/blank \u2192 `null`. Otherwise it must match the permissive syntactic pattern, is lower-cased, and its domain must not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Failures throw `InvalidFieldsException([\"email\"])`.\n\n7. **Map DTO \u2192 Owner + apply normalized values (side-effect)** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`, then `setTelephone(...)` and `setEmail(...)` with the normalized values from steps 4 and 6.\n\n8. **Unique-identity check** \u2014 `requireUniqueIdentity(owner)`. Rejects if any existing owner already has the same normalized telephone (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`). (Despite the \"identity key\" wording, the actual collision test is telephone-only.)\n\n9. **Household-duplicate check (conditional)** \u2014 computes `sharesHousehold = TRUE.equals(dto.getSharesHousehold())`. If **not** sharing, `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate(owner)` runs: only for owners *with* a postcode, rejects if an existing owner shares the computed household id (first 12 hex of SHA-256 over normalized last name + postcode) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException`. Skipped entirely when `sharesHousehold` is set.\n\n10. **Registration-date-not-in-future check** \u2014 `requireRegistrationDateNotInFuture(...)`. A supplied `registrationDate` later than today throws `InvalidFieldsException([\"registrationDate\"])`; `null` is allowed.\n\n11. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day roll (side-effect)** \u2014 effective date = supplied date or `LocalDate.now()` if null; `toBusinessDay(...)` rolls Saturday\u2192Monday (+2) and Sunday\u2192Monday (+1); the result is stored via `setRegistrationDate(...)`.\n\n12. **Daily-limit check** \u2014 `requireDailyLimitNotReached(registrationDate)`. If \u2265 100 owners already share that (business-day-adjusted) registration date, throws `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n13. **Bulk-signup flag (side-effect)** \u2014 `setBulkSignupWarning(isBulkSignup(...))`. Sets `true` when **more than 80** owners already share that registration date (count taken before persisting).\n\n14. **Possible-duplicate detection (side-effect, conditional)** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, `findPossibleDuplicate(owner)` finds the lowest-id existing owner with the same last name (case-insensitive) and postcode but a *different* telephone (only when the new owner has a postcode). Then `setPossibleDuplicate(...)` and `setPossibleDuplicateOf(...)` are set accordingly (flag false / id null when none or when sharing household).\n\n15. **Persist (side-effect)** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`. The owner is written and assigned its id.\n\n16. **Audit log (side-effect)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` emits one line with the new owner's `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel`.\n\n17. **Response assembly (side-effect on response)** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, sets the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, and returns `201 CREATED`.\n\n**Note on ordering:** all validations and duplicate/limit checks run *before* persistence, but they are interleaved with normalizations rather than all up front \u2014 notably address normalization (step 1) happens before the required-field check, telephone/email normalization occur before their uniqueness/persistence use, and the registration date is defaulted and rolled to a business day (step 11) before both the daily-limit check and the bulk-signup flag are evaluated against that adjusted date. The method is **not** `@Transactional`, so the pre-save read-based checks (city capacity, uniqueness, household, daily limit) are not guarded against concurrent inserts."
